University Budget Analytics Dashboard

An Excel + Power BI dashboard concept using sample university budget transactions.


Files


sample_budget_transactions.csv — sample credits and debits by department and date.

department_budgets.csv — allocated budget for each department.

measures.dax — DAX measures to create in Power BI.


Build the dashboard in Power BI


Open Power BI Desktop.

Select Get Data → Text/CSV and import both CSV files.

Set Date to the Date data type and Amount / AllocatedBudget to Decimal or Whole Number.

Create a relationship from department_budgets[Department] to sample_budget_transactions[Department] (one-to-many).

Add the DAX measures from measures.dax.

Suggested visuals:
Cards: Total Credit, Total Debit, Net Balance, Budget Utilised %.
Clustered column chart: Department vs Total Debit.
Line chart: Month vs Total Debit.
Table: Department, Allocated Budget, Total Debit, Budget Utilised %.
Slicers: Department, Date, Type.

Apply conditional formatting to Budget Utilised % (for example, highlight values above 80%).


Excel alternative

Open the transactions CSV in Excel, format it as a table, create PivotTables by Department and Month, and add slicers for Department and Type.


Note

The CSV files contain illustrative sample data, not real university financial records. The dashboard is a reporting prototype.

